# The length of the list is not known. `add` is a declared function that cannot count its arguments and that comes back, so the place hands the list to the one function that every such place shares: a jump,
# without the closure of `add` and without a receiver.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="addAll" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[values]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Void b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@[[values]]:Register({{*}}), runsWithoutFrame, resultConstraints = WarmAny, Terminal|{{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# NONE-LABEL: name="addAll" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: :CallList)
# NONE-NOT: :GetModuleVariable)
# NONE-NOT: Branch(
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# CALLS-LABEL: f2: size=
# CALLS-NEXT: function f{{*}} x1
# CALLS-NEXT: f{{*}}: size=

# The shared function reads the three arguments out of the storage of the list, whichever of the three kinds it is, and calls the typed body of `add`. It returns from that call, and no stack trace lists it.
# A list that is too long, too short or has a hole goes to the stub that calls a value with a list, and only that way makes the closure.
# IR-LABEL: name="addAll"
# IR-NEXT: b0(v0: {{*}}):
# IR-NEXT: [[sum]]: anything = CallDirect v0 function={{*}}[isNeverInlined]
# IR-NEXT: ReturnCall [[sum]]
# IR-LABEL: name="callWithElements" module=- role=OutlinedBody
# IR: [[fits]]: boolean = LessEq {{*}}form=Integers
# IR-NEXT: TestAndBranch [[fits]] -> taken {{*}}(), notTaken [[byValue]]()
# IR-NEXT: [[byValue]]() frequency=Rare:
# IR-NEXT: [[closure]]: f1 = GetModuleVariable variable=g0
# IR-NEXT: [[answer]]: anything = CallList [[closure]], -, v0
# IR-NEXT: Return [[answer]]
# IR: [[isDouble]]: boolean = HasArrayStorage v0 arrayStorage=Double
# IR-NEXT: TestAndBranch [[isDouble]] -> taken {{*}}(| 0), notTaken [[integers]]()
# IR-NEXT: [[integers]]():
# IR-NEXT: [[isInt32]]: boolean = HasArrayStorage v0 arrayStorage=Int32
# IR: = IsElementPresent v0, {{*}} arrayStorage=Double [keyIsIntegral]
# IR-NEXT: TestAndBranch {{*}} -> taken {{*}}(| 0), notTaken [[byValue]]()
# IR: [[first]]: number = GetArrayElement v0, {{*}} arrayStorage=Double level=Expected [keyIsIntegral, isPresent]
# IR: [[second]]: number = GetArrayElement v0, {{*}} arrayStorage=Double level=Expected [keyIsIntegral, isPresent]
# IR: [[third]]: number = GetArrayElement v0, {{*}} arrayStorage=Double level=Expected [keyIsIntegral, isPresent]
# IR-NEXT: [[typed]]: number = CallDirect [[first]], [[second]], [[third]] function=
# IR-NEXT: Return [[typed]]
# IR: = HasArrayStorage v0 arrayStorage=Contiguous
# IR: [[firstInteger]]: i32 = GetArrayElement v0, {{*}} arrayStorage=Int32 level=Expected [keyIsIntegral, isPresent]
# IR: = CallDirect [[firstInteger]], {{*}} function=
# IR: [[firstValue]]: anything = GetArrayElement v0, {{*}} arrayStorage=Contiguous level=Expected [keyIsIntegral, isPresent]
